  "slug": "mongodb-atlas-aws-networking",
  "concept": "MongoDB Atlas AWS Networking",
  "generated": "2026-09-08",
  "summary": "MongoDB Atlas on AWS supports two private networking models: VPC Peering (legacy) and AWS PrivateLink (recommended). Both complement the Network Access List (IP allowlist) for controlling cluster acce",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "MongoDB Atlas on AWS supports two private networking models: VPC Peering (legacy) and AWS PrivateLink (recommended). Both complement the Network Access List (IP allowlist) for controlling cluster access.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#overview",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Private Endpoint Connection String",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The private endpoint-aware connection string has a different hostname:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#private-endpoint-connection-string",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Not the standard mongodb+srv://cluster0.abcde.mongodb.net.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#private-endpoint-connection-string",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Network Access Lists",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Security Groups as access list entries: For applications running in EC2/ECS/Lambda within a VPC, using Security Group IDs as access list entries is more dynamic and avoids managing CIDR ranges.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#network-access-lists",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "DNS/SRV Resolution",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Atlas uses SRV DNS records (_mongodb._tcp.<hostname>) for cluster discovery. When connecting over PrivateLink, verify:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#dnssrv-resolution",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "DNS resolves to private IPs (not public Atlas IPs)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#dnssrv-resolution",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Security groups allow TCP on ports returned by SRV records (typically 1024-65535 for PrivateLink)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#dnssrv-resolution",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Transit Gateway Patterns",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "For centralized networking with many VPCs:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#transit-gateway-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Create Atlas PrivateLink endpoint in a \"hub\" VPC",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#transit-gateway-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Connect hub VPC to AWS Transit Gateway",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#transit-gateway-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "All application VPCs access Atlas via Transit Gateway → hub → PrivateLink",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#transit-gateway-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Route table: 10.0.0.0/8 → Transit Gateway in spoke VPCs",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#transit-gateway-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Transit Gateway also enables cross-account Atlas access without creating separate PrivateLink endpoints per account.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#transit-gateway-patterns",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "AWS KMS Encryption at Rest (BYOK)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Atlas uses IAM role assumption (not IAM user credentials) to access the KMS key. Configure via Atlas Cloud Provider Access (Unified AWS Access) → creates a cross-account IAM role.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#aws-kms-encryption-at-rest-byok",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Failsafe: If KMS is inaccessible, running mongod continues (DEK cached in memory) but will not restart.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#aws-kms-encryption-at-rest-byok",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "AWS EventBridge Integration",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Route Atlas alert events to EventBridge:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#aws-eventbridge-integration",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Atlas UI → Integrations → AWS EventBridge → provide AWS account ID",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#aws-eventbridge-integration",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Atlas creates an EventBridge partner event source",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#aws-eventbridge-integration",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Create EventBridge rule to route events to Lambda, SQS, SNS, etc.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-aws-networking/#aws-eventbridge-integration",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
